= Discussion
*Beyond biology.* Inheritance of learned skill, fleet sleep, perfect replay with
counterfactual physics, rollback and A/B of the self, honest introspection, and
bounded modulators.

*Toward one network.* Organs become learned networks one at a time, then train
jointly with the bus kept as auxiliary outputs, then merge. The brainstem stays innate.

*Limits.* One robot, one indoor garage, little data; copying organs from logs risks
covariate shift, so joint training on surprise is required, not optional.
